{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/141256-the-pantheons-of-1e-scion","id":141256,"title":"The Pantheons of 1E Scion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-17T22:27:59-07:00","id":141256,"title":"The Pantheons of 1E Scion","content":"I'm currently reading Part 2 of Scion Companion and I saw a list of ten pantheons and their scents for the Scent The Divine Knack. Here they are according to the book:<br /> <br /> Aesir<br /> Amatsukami<br /> Atlantis<br /> Atzlanti<br /> Celestial Bureaucracy<br /> Devas<br /> Doekatheon<br /> Loa<br /> Pesedjet<br /> Tuatha De Dannan<br /> <br /> Personally, I was surprised to see the Atlantis pantheon in there. Did this mean that White Wolf considered Atlantis to be the official TENTH pantheon in Scion? Evidence seems to point in that direction, given that the pantheon had a write-up in Demigod, and Companion had a list of the Atlantis purview: Scire. If that's so, then we already have the ten pantheons listed for Scion.<br /> <br /> And for those who mention the Yazata, to me, they seem to be an after-thought pantheon, given that they were given their own book after the main line ended. I don't blame them, considering that the Persians were technically the bullies of the Ancient World. They conquered Egypt by holding cats hostage, and they would have conquered Greece if the Greeks weren't experienced sailors. That's two pantheons who would gladly beat the Yazata up on principle. (Three if they then went into the savannah territories of the Loa.)<br /> <br /> So now there's technically 11 pantheons in Scion, (or more if the WWII pantheons are considered canon past their one-shot story).<br /> <br /> Do you guys think that they'll use the same roster of pantheons for this edition?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T22:42:20-07:00","id":141266,"title":"","content":"They've said there will be more and hopefully Atlantis will not be making a re-appearance. The ones they have are a good cultural selection, even if I'd like to see almost all of them renamed and the Loa revamped to be more like the Orisha and less of a New World Christian-Syncretized version of the older religion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T12:14:34-07:00","id":141730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/141256-the-pantheons-of-1e-scion?p=141266#post141266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They've said there will be more and hopefully Atlantis will not be making a re-appearance. The ones they have are a good cultural selection, even if I'd like to see almost all of them renamed and the Loa revamped to be more like the Orisha and less of a New World Christian-Syncretized version of the older religion.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do realize that the reason why they were &quot;syncretized&quot; was because the Southern gentry of the American South tried to convert the slaves with extreme prejudice, right? That's why they have those names. I wouldn't mind if their Americanized names were nicknames that they picked up. I feel kind of sad that Atlantis might not be an influence in the new ediiton. It's like telling the Lord of the Rings story while omitting plot similiarities to the Nibelung Saga. But that's just me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T13:28:31-07:00","id":141767,"title":"","content":"How about having Atlantis be an influence in Graeco-Roman mythology? Since, ya know.... well that's the origin of the myth, the only real boots-on-the-ground archaeology tie-in. That kinda stuff. <br /> <br /> Instead of just making shit up out of nothing. Which they didn't even do for the Yankee, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T18:52:51-07:00","id":141971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/141256-the-pantheons-of-1e-scion?p=141730#post141730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do realize that the reason why they were &quot;syncretized&quot; was because the Southern gentry of the American South tried to convert the slaves with extreme prejudice, right? That's why they have those names. I wouldn't mind if their Americanized names were nicknames that they picked up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes? What possible relevance does that have to a question of the Loa or the Orisha appearing in Scion2E? The &quot;Americanized&quot; names aren't just names, they're from a different religion, with very different themes and beliefs. The Orishas would have an entirely different roster, PSP, set of Virtues... because they're a different religion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/141256-the-pantheons-of-1e-scion?p=141730#post141730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I feel kind of sad that Atlantis might not be an influence in the new ediiton. It's like telling the Lord of the Rings story while omitting plot similiarities to the Nibelung Saga. But that's just me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Atlantis given in Scion 1E isn't mythology, it's someone's whole-cloth invention that dates back to the grand old year of 2007. If you want to keep Atlantis, use Plato's version (which he also made up, but at least it has some history behind it). It'd make a great Greek Terra Incognita!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T20:15:15-07:00","id":142030,"title":"","content":"With the Atlantis thing being suggested as Terra Incognita, I thinkit would work. It was just the nostalgia of Atlantis being prevalent in mythology that I probably will miss.<br /> <br /> As with the Loa of America being different, in what way? To me, it's the same pantheon and the same rituals and beliefs. It's the names that are different, due to pressure of Southern Christians who wanted to erase anything pagan when it came to their slaves. Placing a saint's name in place of the actual name is basically a smokescreen so that their culture wouldn't be destroyed by White people. If changing a god's name makes him part of a different religion, then there's actually HUNDREDS of religions out there, given that the gods of the pantheons have aliases (AKA). Hell, Brer Rabbit is also known as Coyote of Native American lore. Does that mean that Coyote abandoned the pantheon that Native Americans exalted for the Yankee Pantheon? To me, no. I consider Brer Rabbit and Coyote to be two different personas of the same god. A Loa, whether he's named Damballah or Grandpa Moses, shouldn't make a difference. It's technically the same religion. If there's a difference, then it should be considered a sect of the main religion, just like Baptists and Lutherans are sects of Christianity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T22:49:39-07:00","id":142104,"title":"","content":"But.. that isn't at all how it works generally, or specifically in this case. The voodoo religion, just like palo mayombe, santeria and the other afro-american syncratic religions are their own things, very much separate from their origins. They're not just one single &quot;African&quot; religion with Christianity mixed in. They're normally several different religions from what in some instances are several different ethnic groups in Africa, mixed with Christianity and native American religions, plus a whole bevy of new stuff that evolved to fit the needs of those people. A little bit of in-depth study will show you that the religions practiced in the New World have a great deal <i>in common </i>with the religions from Africa (again, there's lots of those), but they're absolutely not the same. <br /> <br /> You can certainly draw <i>parallels</i> between Eshu and Papa Legba, but they are <i>not</i> the same figure. Read about their stories, their symbolism, their personalities. They're very different figures, though it is easy to see how Legba evolved from stories of Eshu.<br /> <br /> Coyote and B'rer Rabbit aren't the same at all either. First off, because the idea of a single &quot;Coyote&quot; figure is laughable. There are at least a dozen &quot;Coyotes&quot; just like there's tons of European &quot;Storm Gods&quot;. Indra, Zeus, Perun and Thor are not all the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T04:27:28-07:00","id":142227,"title":"","content":"The writers haven't been forthcoming on what the four extra pantheons in Hero 2e will be, even when asked directly if they'd be the Companion+Yazata set.<br /> <br /> Joe Carriker has not ruled out revisiting some of the concepts of the WWII/Atlantean pantheons in 2e at some point.<br /> <br /> <br /> Musing on some things brought up in the thread...<br /> <br /> In 2e, we know that the gods can adopt different personae and join other pantheons (the Greek -&gt; Roman is the major citation here, but Mithras can belong both to the Persian and Roman pantheons, and Guanyin to both China and Japan).<br /> <br /> Now, there's a certain degree of real-world difference involved here - the Roman pantheon may draw heavily on the Greek, but many of its members aren't identical to their Grecian counterparts, and Persian Mithra isn't identical to Roman Mithras. The idea here is that the gods are large enough in themselves to encompass these variants.<br /> <br /> That said, given that the writers aren't treating all equivalent gods as being ultimately the same, there's going to be a cut-off point where a counterpart god in another culture is a separate god in their own right, rather than being an alternate divine persona. Trying to figure out where that point is, is another matter.<br /> <br /> <br /> On another note, I have to wonder if the writers are going to change the Loa as fans expect (that is, making them closer to the Orisha). Vodou is a syncretic faith, formed from several mythologies, not just one. It could be an example of a relatively new pantheon, with members from several pre-existing pantheons - who still belong to said pre-existing pantheons as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T09:00:16-07:00","id":142355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/141256-the-pantheons-of-1e-scion?p=142227#post142227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On another note, I have to wonder if the writers are going to change the Loa as fans expect (that is, making them closer to the Orisha). Vodou is a syncretic faith, formed from several mythologies, not just one. It could be an example of a relatively new pantheon, with members from several pre-existing pantheons - who still belong to said pre-existing pantheons as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be excellent as it would put emphasis on the possibility that PCs can form their own Pantheons, even if they still belong to whatever Pantheon they originated from. It does raise a question though, regarding the PSPs: Assuming they still exist in their current form, are the Scions given access to both the PSP of the joint Pantheon their parents belong to and the original Pantheon they belong to? For example, would a Scion of Zeus/Jupiter have access to both the PSP of the Greco and the Roman Pantheon (assuming they are not the same to begin with)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://emeraldsamurai.com\" target=\"_blank\">Emerald Samurai</a> for my alternative character-sheets for WoD, Scion, Exalted and more.<br /> Like my <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com/EmeraldSamurai\" target=\"_blank\">Facebook page</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/308-skari-dono","name":"Skari-dono","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T09:27:04-07:00","id":142389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/141256-the-pantheons-of-1e-scion?p=142227#post142227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> On another note, I have to wonder if the writers are going to change the Loa as fans expect (that is, making them closer to the Orisha). Vodou is a syncretic faith, formed from several mythologies, not just one. It could be an example of a relatively new pantheon, with members from several pre-existing pantheons - who still belong to said pre-existing pantheons as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be even more complex that than. Voodoo may be syncretic. What religion isn't? Voodoo does have it's own character that takes it far enough afield to set it up as it's own thing or at least partially as it's own thing. The mechanism lies in the mythology proper, the nanchons. It would be interesting to see if they could do something like using that concept to square these questions, e.g. perhaps the Petro Loa are actually the Orisha with a (somewhat, partially) new set of names and the Rada are an example of Scions (of the Petro) coming up and making a sub-pantheon/integral part of the pantheon/etc. that is area specfic.<br /> <br /> Also, unless by &quot;Southern Christians&quot; you mean &quot;French Catholocism&quot; the syncretism of Christianity that went into voodoun had very little to do with US. Voodoo formed in Haiti. Hoodoo, on the other hand is America-grown. And the Loa/Orisha/whatever are even better hidden. Just like the Orisha are much closer to their African counterparts in other transplanted faiths of the Caribbean and South America. <br /> <br /> Personally, I think a flagship product should be a lumper rather than splitter situation. To a point. Greek and Roman need to be combined or else we've lost an entire other pantheon and area of the world to cover a split that is going to be hard to differentiate the major players in (sure there are lots of little gods that are different, but not the main players - Zeus vs. Jupiter is hard mythology to separate, but even though Janus might be cool, but who even knows anything about Fevrus? Jupiter is just a Latinate contraction for &quot;Zeus pater&quot; since Latin didn't even have a &quot;Z&quot; sound) Maybe even some way can be found to integrate Orisha/Loa/etc together enough to present them as one pantheon. (I made my stab at it above). But you can't go &quot;Indo-European&quot; and integrate Zeus/Jupiter with Thor with Perun with Indra with Tarhun with Vahram (possibly) with Taranis (possibly) into &quot;STORM GOD&quot;. That renders the source material that attracts people to the game, meaningless. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T11:46:54-07:00","id":142585,"title":"","content":"I apologize. Scion is the first time I've been exposed to the African pantheon and so I thought that the Loa (or Orisha) was somewhat transplanted here in America by slaves to preserve their culture in a foreign land. I didn't realize that they were separate from African influence as their own entity. So when people say that the Loa isn't African in the way it seems, I say, &quot;Wait a minute. The Loa IS the Orisha. They came from the same culture. Why are they different?&quot; This just proves that I don't know crap about the Loa after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T12:02:01-07:00","id":142592,"title":"","content":"As an afterthought, How would the Loa of the US, react to the Orisha of America, and if they're different, will the Loa be absorbed into the eventual reincarnation of the Yankee Pantheon in 2E?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T12:41:06-07:00","id":142608,"title":"","content":"Oh please for the love of all the gods I hope they do not actually allow the Yankee Pantheon to make the cut. It might be a good example of showing the potential for new pantheons but to me it was just a sad ass thing all around. Out of everything in the World at War section of the Companion book, I only liked a few things. The added gods to the pre-existing pantheons, and Baba Yaga. But Baba Yaga is a pre-existing god from an older Pantheon as well, not some god who was just made up specifically for that section of the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T15:11:33-07:00","id":142700,"title":"","content":"Actually, the Baba Yaga in the book came from the Soviet Pantheon. The Yankee Pantheon is full of the tall-tale characters from stories that sprang up from the 19th and early 20th century United States. If anything, I would think that after Communism ended, that Baba Yaga was absorbed by the Chinese Bureaucracy with their Convert Shen Taiyi ability, along with the other members of the Soviet Pantheon. But that's just me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T18:12:52-07:00","id":142872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/141256-the-pantheons-of-1e-scion?p=142227#post142227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The writers haven't been forthcoming on what the four extra pantheons in Hero 2e will be, even when asked directly if they'd be the Companion+Yazata set.</div> </div> </div> </div>When did we get directly asked this...?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T18:33:42-07:00","id":142898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/141256-the-pantheons-of-1e-scion?p=141266#post141266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They've said there will be more and hopefully Atlantis will not be making a re-appearance. The ones they have are a good cultural selection, even if I'd like to see almost all of them renamed and the Loa revamped to be more like the Orisha and less of a New World Christian-Syncretized version of the older religion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope they keep the power. I really liked the idea of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T16:13:01-07:00","id":143933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/141256-the-pantheons-of-1e-scion?p=142700#post142700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, the Baba Yaga in the book came from the Soviet Pantheon. The Yankee Pantheon is full of the tall-tale characters from stories that sprang up from the 19th and early 20th century United States. If anything, I would think that after Communism ended, that Baba Yaga was absorbed by the Chinese Bureaucracy with their Convert Shen Taiyi ability, along with the other members of the Soviet Pantheon. But that's just me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Baba Yaga was made a part of the Soviet Pantheon, but as it states even in the book as well as from Slavic Mythology, that Baba Yaga was a part of an older Pantheon which has essentially retreated from the world. Much like the Yankee Pantheon, the Soviet Pantheon was mostly made up. While the Yankee Pantheon comes from characters from Tall Tales that sprang up during the 19th and 20th century and is a good example of showing the potential for a new pantheon (For those who would like to create one), Baba Yaga does in fact come from a much older Slavic Faith, they just molded her to fit into the Soviet Pantheon for the purpose of the game. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T18:59:41-07:00","id":144016,"title":"","content":"\u201cAllied Pantheon\u201d (which included figures from British and French folklore as well as Soviet Russia), not \u201cSoviet Pantheon\u201d. I\u2019ll just note, though, that <i>nobody</i>, not even those supporting a return of the Yankee Pantheon in some form or another, seems to be interested in a return of the Allied Pantheon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T00:53:02-07:00","id":144241,"title":"","content":"That's why I think that instead of &quot;Yankee Pantheon&quot; it should be probably be named differently. Having a pantheon based on North America would make the World seem more complete as well as an Austrailian pantheon based on entities of The Dreaming of Aboriginal lore would also complete the world. As far as I know, according to what I gleamed from the odd trivia question, the Koala was responsible for the rainfall that happens in Australia. So Sky and Water? As for the named &quot;Allied Pantheon&quot;, I think that was just for the WWII scenario, as they were dealing with the madness that pervaded the Aesir, Dodekatheon, and Amatsukami pantheons during that time<br /> <br /> So for an Australian pantheon, we could call it the &quot;Dreaming Pantheon&quot; to use the lingo.<br /> <br /> As for North America, the &quot;American Pantheon&quot;?<br /> <br /> Not having something be influential in those two areas seems to me like they are Divine Dead Zones when it comes to the Gods, IMHO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T07:05:20-07:00","id":144447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/141256-the-pantheons-of-1e-scion?p=144241#post144241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for North America, the &quot;American Pantheon&quot;?<br /> <br /> Not having something be influential in those two areas seems to me like they are Divine Dead Zones when it comes to the Gods, IMHO.</div> </div> </div> </div>North America has several Pantheons that would do it justice...the Navajo, the Haida, the Inuit...the list goes on. It is far far from being a dead zone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T08:37:42-07:00","id":144500,"title":"","content":"The United States doesn't have a Pantheon because it has never been a polytheistic society. Tall tales and historical figures just aren't on the same level as actual deities from a living, practiced religion. Fortunately Samudra is right and there were dozens of different, active, polytheistic religions on the North American continent. Any of those can be used to give an &quot;American&quot; Pantheon to Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T09:30:01-07:00","id":144531,"title":"","content":"Religion can be a shifty word to me.<br /> But actual &quot;worship?&quot; I don't know if that word applies to certain Native tribes. Revere? Yes. Worship? Hmm...<br /> <br /> Just thinking out loud, so to speak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T22:25:19-07:00","id":146379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/141256-the-pantheons-of-1e-scion?p=144500#post144500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The United States doesn't have a Pantheon because it has never been a polytheistic society. Tall tales and historical figures just aren't on the same level as actual deities from a living, practiced religion. Fortunately Samudra is right and there were dozens of different, active, polytheistic religions on the North American continent. Any of those can be used to give an &quot;American&quot; Pantheon to Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right about that. I hope that they do that for 2E. As for the other big area, Australia, how can we make a pantheon for that based on the Aboriginal religion of the Dreaming?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T22:38:05-07:00","id":146386,"title":"","content":"Plus will the Loa EVER make a return in 2E? Cause if not, then a certain moderator's name is going to be redundant, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T07:26:45-07:00","id":146702,"title":"","content":"I also wouldn't mind seeing something based on the Sumerian faith which has a name that for the life of me I cannot recall, as well as the Slavic Faith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T07:39:12-07:00","id":146725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Dude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/141256-the-pantheons-of-1e-scion?p=146702#post146702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also wouldn't mind seeing something based on the Sumerian faith which has a name that for the life of me I cannot recall, as well as the Slavic Faith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sumerian = Annunaki and Igigi (insofar as ANY book I have on hand from those classes or any source I can find, they weren't called the Annuna)<br /> Slavic = gotta make one up, &quot;bog&quot; is the Slavic word for god, but there isn't enough material remaining to see if they had a name for themselves or the BIG IMPORTANT GODS - like calling the whole Egyptian Pantheon, the Pesedjet, which is just the Greater Ennead (the usual suspects, Isis, Osris, etc., but doesn't include guys like Min or Bes or the Graeco-Roman gods the Dodekatheon when that's just the twelve on Olympus (again, all the usual suspects, but not including Hades)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}